      "raw_text": "Here is the step-by-step solution to the problem:\n\n**Step 1: Calculate the total number of apples.**\nUncle Franky ordered 2 boxes, and each box contains 40 apples.\n$$40 \\text{ apples/box} \\times 2 \\text{ boxes} = 80 \\text{ apples}$$\n\n**Step 2: Determine how many packs can be made.**\nHe plans to pack the apples in groups of 8. We need to divide the total number of apples by the number of apples per pack.\n$$80 \\text{ total apples} \\div 8 \\text{ apples/pack} = 10 \\text{ packs}$$\n\n**Conclusion:**\nUncle Franky can make 10 packs of apples.\n\n#### 10<|im_end|>",
